      "letterAudio": "audio/el/letters/el-tonos.mp3",
      "memoryTrick": "The tonos is a small diagonal line above a vowel that tells you which syllable to stress. Every Greek word with more than one syllable has exactly one tonos. Think of it as a built-in pronunciation guide — it's like the bold syllable in a dictionary entry!"
