    {
      "id": "el-dialytika",
      "char": "ϊ ϋ ΐ ΰ",
      "name": "Dialytika (Diaeresis)",
      "romanization": "indicates a vowel is pronounced separately, not as part of a diphthong",
      "ipa": "/i/ (separated from preceding vowel)",
      "letterAudio": "audio/el/letters/el-dialytika.mp3",
      "memoryTrick": "Two dots placed over ι or υ, just like the German umlaut or the diaeresis in English 'naïve'. It tells you to pronounce the vowel separately — so 'αϊ' sounds like 'ah-ee' not 'eh'. When combined with tonos (ΐ, ΰ), it means the vowel is both stressed and separate."
